title: Day6_Hermes_Intro
tags:
---
<<Scene new_dining_area>>
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Hermes" "Hermes 3_4" "right" "bottom" #023020>>

Aelius: Hermes, welcome in!
Hermes: Hey, Aelius; how’re you doing today?
Aelius: Pretty good, actually. I’m settling in well, I think.
Hermes: Glad to hear it.
Aelius: I forgot to ask yesterday, did you… manage to deliver the food to my mom the other day?
Hermes: Of course I did. I wouldn’t be the messenger of the gods if I flaked on my duties, after all.
Hermes: She appreciated having a nice warm meal, said it tasted like home again.
Aelius: [Positive] Good, I'm glad.
Hermes: She also asked me to tell you she misses ya.
Hermes: Don’t sweat it, it was no trouble.
Aelius: Well, how’re you, Hermes?
Hermes: Doing just fine. It’s a lovely day out today, so it’s been a breeze doing my deliveries.
Hermes: (Mumbling) Too damn many, though...
Aelius: Listen, Hermes, I wanted to talk to you about something…
Hermes: Oh? Do tell.
Aelius: It might not be my place, but I can tell something’s up.
Aelius: You’re acting happy-go-lucky, but I can see through you somewhat well at this point. But also… I get it.

-> There’s been times where I’m pretty swamped with expectations as well. (deference)
    <<AddHermesAffinity 2>>
    Aelius: [Negative] When my mom got ill, I was the only one there who could take care of her.
    Aelius: [Negative] It’s really hard sometimes, having something so important solely rely on you.
    Hermes: Yeah, I get that all too well, kid.
    Hermes:  It’s not always easy, but we just gotta keep moving forward, I suppose.
    Aelius: Yeah. But there’s also no harm in letting others help out a bit.
-> I can get how humor is pretty important for staying positive. (humorous)
    <<AddHermesAffinity 3>>
    Aelius: [Negative] Sometimes it’s easier to joke about the heavy stuff than to be honest with myself about how much it hurts sometimes.
    Hermes: I tend to be the same. Being gloomy doesn’t help me out, so I might as well laugh about it.
    Hermes: That isn’t always easy, though, I suppose.
    Aelius: (Dryly) For real, tell me about it.
    Aelius: It’s all I felt for a bit, after my mom…
    Hermes: Yeah, I can imagine, kid.
-> It can be so frustrating dealing with someone who doesn’t care as much. (aggressive)
    <<AddHermesAffinity 2>>
    Aelius: [Negative] With my absent father, everything fell on my shoulders – while still trying to stay afloat myself. Happened to me a lot after my mom got sick…
    Aelius: [Negative] I’d imagine you’ve… experienced similar.
    Hermes: ...
    Hermes: … Yeah, I have – where the only way to get through is keeping a smile on my face.
    Hermes: I rarely get to see my mother. You and I are kindred spirits in that regard.
    Aelius: Seems so.

Hermes: Well...
Hermes: Thanks for opening up Aelius.
Hermes: It’s actually… kinda nice talking about it with someone who gets it.
Aelius: [Positive] Yeah, same here, honestly.
Hermes: Yeah, but… anywho! I’m starving after all of that chit chat.
Aelius: [Smirk] Of course you are. What can I get for you today?
Hermes: Hmm, how about an <b>Erymanthian Boar Sandwich</b>? That sounds like just the thing I need right now.
Aelius: Fresh boar sammy, coming right up.

// COOKING GAME HERE
<<AddHermesAffinity 2>>
